Z||000007||terryk||03-12-2000||09:59 PM||||Hooker at one time made headers for the X-11, PN 2146. These are Y pipe style, not wrap -around.<P>They might be willing to crank out another run. Or, you might find some shop with a set.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||03-12-2000||10:05 PM||||When I put the 3.4 in my GT, I am going to use the camaro factory manifolds. It will require some creative pipe bending, but my muffler guy looked and said that it can be done. The forward bank will be routed almost in the stock location while the rear bank will come off the engine, curve back around toward the passenger side of the the car and join into the pipe from the front bank just before the muffler. The reason I chose to keep the 3.4 manifolds is the size of the pipe in much bigger than that of the 2.8- the pipe from one bank is as large as the y-pipe on the Fiero. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||03-13-2000||06:38 AM||||Cooter, document your method, you just might be pioneering a new exhaust system. Bigger manifolds would generally mean more flow, possibly at a slight loss of back-pressure. This would mean you might lose a little torque, but gain a healthy dose of ponies due to better breathing. With the higher torque of the 3.4 just from it being a larger displacement, that would be a good trade off. ||||reg||1
